# Flow past a cylinder, 3D.  Schaefer et al. (1996), benchmark 3D-2.
#
# The inlet profile is the benchmark's product of two parabolas across the square section:
#   U(y,z) = 16 * Umax * y*z*(0.41-y)*(0.41-z) / 0.41^4,  Umax = 0.45 m/s.
# The cylinder spans the full width, so it is an infinite cylinder about z capped by the
# spanwise walls.

sampling corner

boundary xmin inflow  u="16*0.45*y*z*(0.41-y)*(0.41-z)/(0.41^4)"  clamp_negative=1
boundary xmax pressure_outlet
boundary ymin noslip
boundary ymax noslip
boundary zmin noslip
boundary zmax noslip

region solid cylinder axis=z center=(0.2,0.2) radius=0.05
